power: supply: max77705_charger: report AICL, do not step the input limit

The charger regulates its input voltage in hardware. The AICL handler
additionally stepped CHGIN_LIM down until AICL_OK was set. On the Galaxy
Tab S8+ under a 5 V 3 A PD contract, with the CCIC setting the input
current itself (AUTOIBUS), AICL_OK stayed clear and the handler walked
CHGIN_LIM from 3000 mA to its 100 mA floor within ten seconds while the
battery kept taking 1.4-1.6 A: the register was not what limited the
input, and the stepping only fought the CCIC. With the OTG boost on it
never settled at all (see max77705-charger-aicl-bounded). Report the
event and leave the limit to the hardware and to whoever set it.

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
index 8c6615e95..89e954262 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max77705_charger.c
@@ -41,48 +41,19 @@ static enum power_supply_property max77705_charger_props[] = {
 	POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_INPUT_CURRENT_LIMIT,
 };
 
+/*
+ * The charger regulates its input voltage in hardware (VCHGIN_REG); this
+ * only reports it. Stepping CHGIN_LIM down from here fights the CCIC,
+ * which sets the input current itself under a PD contract (AUTOIBUS):
+ * AICL_OK then stays clear and the limit was walked to its floor while
+ * the input current was unchanged. With the OTG boost running, AICL is
+ * the boost's own VBUS on CHGIN and never settles at all.
+ */
 static irqreturn_t max77705_aicl_irq(int irq, void *irq_drv_data)
 {
 	struct max77705_charger_data *chg = irq_drv_data;
-	unsigned int regval, irq_status, mode;
-	int err;
-
-	/*
-	 * With the OTG boost running, CHGIN sees the boost's own VBUS and
-	 * AICL never settles; stepping the limit down would never end and
-	 * would hold the shared MFD interrupt thread.
-	 */
-	err = regmap_field_read(chg->rfield[MAX77705_MODE], &mode);
-	if (err < 0 || (mode & MAX77705_OTG_CTRL) == MAX77705_OTG_CTRL)
-		return IRQ_HANDLED;
-
-	err = regmap_read(chg->regmap, MAX77705_CHG_REG_INT_OK, &irq_status);
-	if (err < 0)
-		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 
-	// irq is fiered at the end of current decrease sequence too
-	// early check AICL_I bit to guard against that excess irq call
-	while (!(irq_status & BIT(MAX77705_AICL_I))) {
-		err = regmap_field_read(chg->rfield[MAX77705_CHG_CHGIN_LIM], &regval);
-		if (err < 0)
-			return IRQ_HANDLED;
-
-		/* codes 0-3 are all the 100 mA minimum; stop there */
-		if (regval <= 3)
-			return IRQ_HANDLED;
-
-		regval--;
-
-		err = regmap_field_write(chg->rfield[MAX77705_CHG_CHGIN_LIM], regval);
-		if (err < 0)
-			return IRQ_HANDLED;
-
-		msleep(AICL_WORK_DELAY_MS);
-
-		err = regmap_read(chg->regmap, MAX77705_CHG_REG_INT_OK, &irq_status);
-		if (err < 0)
-			return IRQ_HANDLED;
-	}
+	power_supply_changed(chg->psy_chg);
 
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
